!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/validate/invalid/a-dependent-field-written-before-its-sibling-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/validate-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-DATA] §2.5, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2"
  description: """
    A record's field order is insignificant but for one exception: a free sibling, neither pinned nor a discriminator,
    precedes the field that depends on it, as a `!tag` precedes the value it types, so a reader never holds a value it
    cannot yet type. `cell.kind` is free, and `v` is written before it, so `v` is refused, naming both.
    """
  error: {
    category: validation
    path: "/v"
  }
}
